  clock: 2  # 965b
  nonce: 965b  # 965b
  message: "DISCLOSURE HALF SHIPPED in PR #482 (dev 30370c4cd6). Status deliberately\nUNCHANGED at violated -- see \"WHY NOT SATISFIED\" below.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE, re-run on the MERGED tree, this item's own filed repro,\nunmodified:\n\n  ! [host-secret-no-network]  Verdict: confirmed_with_caveats\n    CAVEAT (untyped_receiver): ... At 1 call site(s) -- leak.py:12 sendall()\n    -- a method the network sink catalogue declares is called on a receiver\n    whose type could not be determined, so a flow reaching that sink could\n    neither be constructed nor ruled out.\n  x [host-secret-no-host-fs]  Verdict: violated        <- control, same run\n\nWas bare \"confirmed\" / \"No unsanitized host_secret data reaches network\nzone.\" ARM 2 (sock: socket.socket, otherwise identical) is STILL violated --\na typed receiver is SEEN, not caveated. Zone scoping holds on real code: of\nsix generic taint claims only the network one acquires the site-naming\ncaveat. Falsifiability control (a fixture with no untyped method call at all)\nreturns rc 0, six bare confirmed, ZERO caveats -- so this is not a blanket\ndowngrade.\n\nTHE ASYMMETRY, which is what this item is actually about, is closed. One\ninvocation over the same file now discloses on BOTH arms, names the same\nsite, and reports the SAME denominator. Before, the boundary arm named\nleak.py:12 sendall() and the taint arm certified \"no host_secret reaches\nnetwork zone\" two verdicts later -- with a tick on the silent one and a\nwarning on the disclosing one, so the arm that had looked LESS read as the\nmore confident. Artifact: inv_nuhun_asymmetry_one_run_08222026.log in the lab\nnotebook.\n\n*** THIS ITEM'S root_cause FIELD IS INCOMPLETE AND MISLEADS TOWARD THE WRONG\nFIX. *** It names one suppression -- _lookup_named_entry dropping method-kind\nrows with no module hint -- and there are TWO, both firing, so a fix aimed at\nthe named one changes nothing at all. gate_named_entry refuses an untyped\nmethod call OUTRIGHT at its first line (call_construct == \"method\"); even\nwith that line deleted, its non_method filter still refuses, because the\nindex bucket for sendall holds only method-kind rows. Verified at the unit on\nthe shipped catalogue: _lookup_named_entry(hits, \"sendall\", None) -> None,\n(..., \"external\") -> None, (..., \"socket.socket\") -> the network TaintSink.\n\nAND BOTH REFUSALS ARE LOAD-BEARING, NOT BUGS. They are the deliberate closure\nof INV-tapat and INV-maluk, both satisfied -- and INV-maluk was REOPENED in\nJune 2026 precisely because taint.py's sink matcher was the THIRD consumer\nthat ignored the rule (the WI-razol ~5541-violation cascade). INV-maluk's\nstatement forbids matching a method-kind primitive on the unfiltered\nshort-name fallback, in those words. So the flow CANNOT be recovered by\nwidening the gate; it can only be recovered by TYPING THE RECEIVER, which is\nINV-fibis's recall half. The description already said this item is not asking\nfor a recall widening, and that reading is correct -- the root_cause field is\nthe part that is wrong. Any future agent reading root_cause alone will try to\nrelax the gate and will regress two satisfied invariants.\n\nWHY NOT SATISFIED. The statement requires a confirmed taint verdict to be\n\"backed by an analysis that COULD HAVE CONSTRUCTED the flow it denies\". The\nanalysis still cannot construct it. What changed is that such a verdict is no\nlonger reported as bare confirmed. That is exactly INV-fibis's open\ndisposition question, now posed identically here -- so ONE OWNER RULING\nSETTLES BOTH: does \"backed by an analysis that could have classified/\nconstructed\" hold when the analysis still cannot, but no longer claims to\nhave? Deferring to the owner rather than closing on my own reading of my own\nfix.\n\nCOLLATERAL FOUND, AND IT IS THE INTERESTING PART. Every claim in\ndocs/hypergumbo.claims.yaml is a TAINT claim, so hypergumbo's own security\nself-proof was silent about this and PR #481 (the boundary half) never\ntouched it. All 18 self-claims moved. The check-self-claims gate caught it;\nthe snapshot was re-recorded only after reviewing exactly what that gate warns\nit is ratifying: 0 verdicts moved, 0 credited_flows moved, 18 caveat-only\nadditions, 0 removals. The disclosure's noise is nameable rather than hidden\n-- of the 119 sites raised against each host_fs claim, 63 are .replace(),\noverwhelmingly str.replace (the literal INV-maluk collision, which the gate\ncorrectly refuses to MATCH but can and now does DISCLOSE). The rest is not\nnoise: mkdir 19, write_text 12, write 11, unlink 9, rename/truncate/touch;\nthe network claim raises write 11, close 6, send_json 1. SECURITY.md now\nstates the bound its \"Known limitations\" had left unquantified: 6,541 of\n9,267 method call sites (70.6%) in hypergumbo's own tree have a receiver the\nanalysis could not type.\n\nNOT MEASURED, unchanged from the item's own list: any language other than\npython; how many real repos' taint verdicts acquire a caveat (this is\nfixtures plus hypergumbo's own tree, not a corpus census); whether the source\nside has an independent hole; and whether the same shape reproduces for\nuntrusted_input sources rather than host_secret."  # 965b
